; MOCHI recovery manifest, schema version 3 (ratification items R3, R5). Key 13 and
; the provenance reason are FROZEN with R5 (2026-10-11); the rest is restated
; from R3's draft and freezes with R3.
; Decisions: spec Annex B.2.10 (D20), rule 6 and 10; Annex B D10 item 3
; ("key-envelope references join both manifest kinds in the phases that
; introduce them, each as a new manifest schema version"), D18.
;
; Schema 3 is used EXACTLY for the manifests of an Encrypted-profile archive:
; it is schema 2 with key 13 added and required. Readers accept schemas 1, 2,
; and 3. A schema-3 manifest in an archive whose descriptor does not list
; feature 1, or a schema-1 or schema-2 manifest in one that does, is
; RECORD_INVALID.
;
; A manifest of an Encrypted archive is stored SEALED (sealed-object-v0, kinds
; 2 and 3): this schema describes the PLAINTEXT, which only a reader holding
; the data key can see. Features (key 9) list 1.
;
; Schema 2 (docs/schemas/recovery-manifest-v2.cddl) is restated here with its
; code-defined key 12 (provenance), which that file does not yet draw. In
; schema 3 and 2 alike: key 11 is required (an empty array/state is allowed);
; key 12 is allowed in delta(0) of a rewritten archive only.
;
; Key 13 (new):
;   * delta: key operations, applied in order after the namespace operations
;     and before the retention operations, atomically, each judged against the
;     state the previous one left. add: the envelope ID must not be in the
;     set. remove: it must be, and the set must not become empty. A commit's
;     key 11 envelope set (commit-record-v2.cddl) MUST equal the replayed set
;     after this delta, checked wherever a manifest is replayed with a key.
;     Commit 0's delta lists one add per initial envelope.
;   * snapshot: the complete set of valid envelope IDs, strictly increasing
;     bytewise, equal to the replayed set at that commit.
;   A rewrap (rekey --add-passphrase / --remove-passphrase) is a commit whose
;   delta carries key operations and typically nothing else. It is the
;   rewrap audit record (spec 14.4). It never changes the data key.
; Key 12 provenance gains key 3 in schema 3 (the re-encryption audit record):
;   reason 0 = collection or compaction, 1 = re-encryption (rekey --reencrypt).
;   Every rewrite of an Encrypted archive creates a new data key (D20 item 10),
;   so the DEK change is implied by any provenance; reason says why.

manifest = delta-manifest / snapshot-manifest

delta-manifest = {
  0: 3,
  1: archive-id,
  2: seq,
  3: opt-parent,
  4: 0,                       ; kind: delta
  5: [* chunk],
  6: [* file-version],
  7: [* op],
  8: [],
  9: [1],                     ; required features
  10: txid,
  11: [* retention-op],       ; required in schema 3 (may be empty)
  ? 12: provenance,           ; delta(0) of a rewritten archive only
  13: [* key-op],             ; required in schema 3 (may be empty)
}

snapshot-manifest = {
  0: 3,
  1: archive-id,
  2: seq,
  3: null,
  4: 1,                       ; kind: snapshot
  5: [* chunk],
  6: [* file-version],
  7: [],
  8: [* entry],
  9: [1],
  10: txid,
  11: retention-state,        ; required in schema 3 (may be empty)
  ? 12: provenance,
  13: key-state,              ; required, non-empty
}

key-op = add-key / remove-key
add-key = [0, envelope-id]
remove-key = [1, envelope-id]
key-state = [+ envelope-id]   ; strictly increasing bytewise, at most 16

provenance = {
  0: archive-id,              ; source archive ID
  1: [+ [seq, hash32]],       ; per new commit: source sequence, source commit ID; strictly increasing
  2: [* seq],                 ; collected source snapshots; strictly increasing, each before the source head and not kept
  ? 3: 0 / 1,                 ; schema 3 only: 0 collection or compaction, 1 re-encryption. Absent = 0
}

; chunk, file-version, extent, attributes, op, entry, retention-op and
; retention-state are exactly as in recovery-manifest-v2.cddl, with ONE
; difference for chunk: key 2 (protection) is 1 (AEAD) for every chunk of an
; Encrypted archive, key 1 (encoding) stays 0 and describes the sealed
; plaintext (one Zstandard frame), key 3 (stored length) is the length of the
; whole sealed frame (8 + 64 + the zstd frame), key 4 (stored-object hash)
; covers the whole sealed frame, and key 7 (dependencies) is EMPTY (the data
; key is archive-wide, not per chunk; dependency kind 1 stays reserved).
chunk = {
  0: hash32,
  1: 0,
  2: 1,
  3: uint,
  4: hash32,
  5: uint,
  6: hash32,
  7: [],
  8: opt-offset,
}
opt-offset = uint / null
opt-parent = parent / null
parent = { 0: seq, 1: hash32 }

archive-id = bstr .size 32
envelope-id = bstr .size 16
txid = bstr .size 16
hash32 = bstr .size 32
seq = uint
